{"a1":[{"k":"title","cap":"Smallest Window Covering All Letters","say":"Let's solve Smallest Window Covering All Letters, using the Sliding Window approach.","card":{"title":"Smallest Window Covering All Letters","sub":"Sliding Window · Hard","pattern":"sliding-window"}},{"k":"problem","cap":"Given strings s and t, return the shortest substring of s that contains every character of t (counting duplicates). If none exists return \"\". The answer is unique when it exists.","card":{"lines":["Given strings s and t, return the shortest substring of s that contains every character of t (counting duplicates). If none exists return \"\". The answer is unique when it exists."]}},{"k":"example","cap":"For example, with s = \"ADOBECODEBANC\", t = \"ABC\", the answer is \"BANC\".","say":"For example, with s equals \"ADOBECODEBANC\", t equals \"ABC\", the answer is \"BANC\".","card":{"lines":["Input: s = \"ADOBECODEBANC\", t = \"ABC\"","Output: \"BANC\""]}},{"k":"idea","cap":"Exactly the minimum-window template: need counts what t still requires and missing counts how many characters are outstanding.","card":{"pattern":"sliding-window","name":"Sliding Window"}},{"k":"idea","cap":"Add s[right]. While nothing is missing, record the window, then give back s[left] and move left; if that breaks the cover, the shrinking stops.","say":"Add s at right. While nothing is missing, record the window, then give back s at left and move left; if that breaks the cover, the shrinking stops.","card":{"pattern":"sliding-window","name":"Sliding Window"}},{"k":"trace","cap":"Let's walk through it with s = \"ADOBECODEBANC\", t = \"ABC\".","say":"Let's walk through it with s equals \"ADOBECODEBANC\", t equals \"ABC\".","st":{"arrays":[{"n":"s","v":["A","D","O","B","E","C","O","D","E","B","A","N","C"],"p":[{"l":"left","i":0},{"l":"right","i":0}],"w":[0,0]}],"vars":[{"k":"missing","v":"2"},{"k":"min_len","v":"14"}]}},{"k":"step","cap":"'A' was needed. Still missing: 2.","ln":{"python":8,"java":7},"st":{"arrays":[{"n":"s","v":["A","D","O","B","E","C","O","D","E","B","A","N","C"],"p":[{"l":"left","i":0},{"l":"right","i":0}],"w":[0,0]}],"vars":[{"k":"missing","v":"2"},{"k":"min_len","v":"14"}]}},{"k":"step","cap":"'B' was needed. Still missing: 1.","ln":{"python":8,"java":7},"st":{"arrays":[{"n":"s","v":["A","D","O","B","E","C","O","D","E","B","A","N","C"],"p":[{"l":"left","i":0},{"l":"right","i":3}],"w":[0,3]}],"vars":[{"k":"missing","v":"1"},{"k":"min_len","v":"14"}]}},{"k":"step","cap":"'C' was needed. Still missing: 0.","ln":{"python":8,"java":7},"st":{"arrays":[{"n":"s","v":["A","D","O","B","E","C","O","D","E","B","A","N","C"],"p":[{"l":"left","i":0},{"l":"right","i":5}],"w":[0,5]}],"vars":[{"k":"missing","v":"0"},{"k":"min_len","v":"14"}]}},{"k":"step","cap":"'ADOBEC' covers everything. Shortest so far: 6.","ln":{"python":12,"java":9},"st":{"arrays":[{"n":"s","v":["A","D","O","B","E","C","O","D","E","B","A","N","C"],"p":[{"l":"left","i":0},{"l":"right","i":5}],"w":[0,5]}],"vars":[{"k":"missing","v":"0"},{"k":"min_len","v":"6"}]}},{"k":"step","cap":"Giving back 'A' breaks the cover.","ln":{"python":15,"java":10},"st":{"arrays":[{"n":"s","v":["A","D","O","B","E","C","O","D","E","B","A","N","C"],"p":[{"l":"left","i":0},{"l":"right","i":5}],"w":[0,5]}],"vars":[{"k":"missing","v":"1"},{"k":"min_len","v":"6"}]}},{"k":"step","cap":"'A' was needed. Still missing: 0.","ln":{"python":8,"java":7},"st":{"arrays":[{"n":"s","v":["A","D","O","B","E","C","O","D","E","B","A","N","C"],"p":[{"l":"left","i":1},{"l":"right","i":10}],"w":[1,10]}],"vars":[{"k":"missing","v":"0"},{"k":"min_len","v":"6"}]}},{"k":"step","cap":"Giving back 'C' breaks the cover.","ln":{"python":15,"java":10},"st":{"arrays":[{"n":"s","v":["A","D","O","B","E","C","O","D","E","B","A","N","C"],"p":[{"l":"left","i":5},{"l":"right","i":10}],"w":[5,10]}],"vars":[{"k":"missing","v":"1"},{"k":"min_len","v":"6"}]}},{"k":"step","cap":"'C' was needed. Still missing: 0.","ln":{"python":8,"java":7},"st":{"arrays":[{"n":"s","v":["A","D","O","B","E","C","O","D","E","B","A","N","C"],"p":[{"l":"left","i":6},{"l":"right","i":12}],"w":[6,12]}],"vars":[{"k":"missing","v":"0"},{"k":"min_len","v":"6"}]}},{"k":"step","cap":"'EBANC' covers everything. Shortest so far: 5.","ln":{"python":12,"java":9},"st":{"arrays":[{"n":"s","v":["A","D","O","B","E","C","O","D","E","B","A","N","C"],"p":[{"l":"left","i":8},{"l":"right","i":12}],"w":[8,12]}],"vars":[{"k":"missing","v":"0"},{"k":"min_len","v":"5"}]}},{"k":"step","cap":"'BANC' covers everything. Shortest so far: 4.","ln":{"python":12,"java":9},"st":{"arrays":[{"n":"s","v":["A","D","O","B","E","C","O","D","E","B","A","N","C"],"p":[{"l":"left","i":9},{"l":"right","i":12}],"w":[9,12]}],"vars":[{"k":"missing","v":"0"},{"k":"min_len","v":"4"}]}},{"k":"step","cap":"Giving back 'B' breaks the cover.","ln":{"python":15,"java":10},"st":{"arrays":[{"n":"s","v":["A","D","O","B","E","C","O","D","E","B","A","N","C"],"p":[{"l":"left","i":9},{"l":"right","i":12}],"w":[9,12]}],"vars":[{"k":"missing","v":"1"},{"k":"min_len","v":"4"}]}},{"k":"done","cap":"The answer is \"BANC\".","st":{"arrays":[{"n":"s","v":["A","D","O","B","E","C","O","D","E","B","A","N","C"],"p":[{"l":"left","i":9},{"l":"right","i":12}],"w":[9,12]}],"vars":[{"k":"missing","v":"1"},{"k":"min_len","v":"4"}]}},{"k":"complexity","cap":"Time complexity is O(n + m) and extra space is O(1). Each character enters and leaves the window at most once; the count table has a fixed alphabet size.","say":"Time complexity is O of n plus m and extra space is O of one. Each character enters and leaves the window at most once; the count table has a fixed alphabet size.","card":{"time":"O(n + m)","space":"O(1)"}},{"k":"outro","cap":"That's the Sliding Window approach. Now try writing it yourself, in Java or Python!"}]}